<!--
  Slide 01 — Title
  Type: title-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from
  acceleration/data/metrics.json and acceleration/data/inflection.json):
    {{DATE_RANGE_HUMAN}}      Repository date range covered by the analysis,
                              rendered as "YYYY-MM-DD → YYYY-MM-DD" (ISO
                              dates separated by U+2192 RIGHTWARDS ARROW
                              with single spaces). Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"environment.first_commit_date"
                              and metrics.json:"environment.last_commit_date".
                              Example: "2022-06-06 → 2026-05-15".
    {{INFLECTION_DATE}}       Detected inflection date (ISO YYYY-MM-DD).
                              Sourced from inflection.json:"date". See
                              AAP §0.3.1.2 (Inflection Detection Decision
                              Flow) for the two-candidate algorithm
                              (earliest AI co-author trailer + sharpest
                              sustained velocity inflection). Example:
                              "2026-02-25".
    {{INFLECTION_METHOD}}     Detection method recorded by
                              detect_inflection.py. Sourced from
                              inflection.json:"method". One of
                              "convergent_evidence" | "single_signal" |
                              "earliest_ai_trailer" | "insufficient_signal"
                              per AAP §0.3.1.2. Example:
                              "convergent_evidence".
    {{GENERATED_TIMESTAMP}}   Report generation timestamp in UTC, rendered
                              as "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM UTC". Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"environment.extraction_timestamp"
                              (also written to run_manifest.json). Example:
                              "2026-05-22 14:00 UTC".
  Required non-text visual: Lucide icon "rocket" (the primary title-slide
  visual, per the file-creation spec). Two additional Lucide icons
  ("calendar", "git-branch") accompany the metadata lines for visual
  consistency with the icon-prefixed paragraph style used elsewhere in
  the deck (e.g., slide_04_inflection.html.tmpl).

  Authority:
    - AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory enumerates slide_01_title.html.tmpl as
      the first slide template; "Per-slide HTML templates for the
      reveal.js deck (Title, Section Divider, Content, Closing variants)").
    - AAP §0.4.2 ("Per-slide HTML templates for the reveal.js deck
      (Title, Section Divider, Content, Closing variants)" — this file
