    - Metadata labels "Period:", "Inflection:", "Method:", "Generated:"
      are neutral status descriptors. No comparative qualifiers appear
      in the rendered title-slide body.

  Body word count (excluding tokens):
    Eyebrow "Acceleration Analysis · Formbricks" (4)
    + Heading "Development Acceleration" (2)
    + Subheading "Baseline vs Post-Introduction" (3)
    + Metadata labels "Period:" (1) + "Inflection:" (1) + "Method:" (1)
      + "Generated:" (1)
    ≈ 13 words. Title slides are exempt from the content-slide 40-word
    body cap, but this slide stays well under it regardless.

  Verification (verify_report.py asserts):
    - Exactly one top-level <section> with class="title-slide".
    - At least one <i data-lucide="…"> icon (non-text visual gate —
      this template has three: calendar, git-branch, rocket).
    - Zero emoji codepoints in the U+1F300–U+1F9FF, U+2600–U+27BF,
      and U+1FA70–U+1FAFF ranges. The middle dot U+00B7 in the
      eyebrow and the U+2192 RIGHTWARDS ARROW in the
      {{DATE_RANGE_HUMAN}} substitution are math/punctuation
      codepoints outside all three emoji ranges.
    - No HTML preformatted-code fenced blocks, no script tags, no link
      tags, no inline style tags, no external href/src references.
    - All four tokens ({{DATE_RANGE_HUMAN}}, {{INFLECTION_DATE}},
      {{INFLECTION_METHOD}}, {{GENERATED_TIMESTAMP}}) appear unsubstituted
